{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481026-setting-hack-minor-arcana-and-realms","id":1481026,"title":"Setting Hack:Minor Arcana (and Realms)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-13T16:52:59-07:00","id":1481026,"title":"Setting Hack:Minor Arcana (and Realms)","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hi guys,this is a setting hack inspired by the concept of Minor Sphere from the Ascension's Storytellers Handbook and the idea of alternate settings from the Mage Chronicler's Guide. I hope you enjoy it!<br /> Minor Realms</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There are many differences of opinions between the awakened. One might argue that they wouldn't be awakened if there weren't any differences. But perhaps the sharpest divide between Mages of all factions is the difference between minor and major supernal realms? In this world there are infinite supernal realms,but the five main ones are far more common than the others. Making mages who awaken to a minor watchtower seem as lesser by those of the dice towers. But what if anything makes the minor Realms truly minor? The answer,at least according to some Mages, is that minor Realms have minor Arcana. Arcana that are only useful sometimes. Defenders of equality between Mages say that in the right situation,a minor arcana is just as powerful as any other.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Let's take a look at the setting hack rules:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minor Arcana work through the same practices as any other,but they are based at far lesser universal concepts than the arcana of the major Realms. Things like Fire,Gravity,Heroism, Light </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minor arcana are grouped in supernal realms with two Major Arcana and one inferior one. Like the major ones. Mages awaken to those Realms a little less usually than to the major ones</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minor Arcana work on all 13 practices,and they have many aspects that sometime overlap,the arcanum of Light ans Fire have many effects in common.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The biggest argument to be made to say that the minor arcana are just as important as the more universal ones,is that everything a major arcana has,a minor has. Gravity as an Aeon,an Exarch,Emanation Realms,Supernal Creatures etc\u2026.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">All Arcana exist in all realms. You can see the Arcanum of Water in Stygia,all you gotta do is look.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the terms of game mechanics,I'll start with a minor Arcanum and walk you through through its Practices</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Minor Arcanum: Fire</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Purview: Light, Growth, Ephemeral Entities with Influence(fire), renewal.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Initiate</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Compelling fire spells can budget flames one way or the other,inspire personal growth on some already inclined to it</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Knowing fire spells can tell you quite a lot of info about literal or metaphorical flames</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unveiling Fire spells show you the way to fire and the things under it's purview</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apprentice:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ruling spells let you command fire related ephemeral entities,and flames themselves</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shielding spells will protect you from being burned in all ways of the word</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ceiling spells simply make fire hard to find and understand</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Disciple</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fraying spells can weaken flames,make them more disperse</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Perfecting spells makes fire and those under it's purview much more closer than its Supernal analogue</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weaving spells might let you turn things not related to fire into things that are</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Adept</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unraveling let you turn fire and those under it's purview into near nothing</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unveiling spells show fire where it could almost never exist</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Master</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Making and unmaking spells straight up can create or uncreate anything fire related</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Worth of fire arcanum is one of the most debated. Many Thyrsus and Obrimos say</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;Fire arcanum? That's bullshit, I can do anything you can do with Spirit and Forces&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And those who awakened to realms with Fire as a Major Arcanum usually answer having a arcanum with such a specialized purview has it's Advantages</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sample Spells For The Fire Arcanum</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Burning Stare (Fire \u25cf)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:knowing</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor:Potency</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Medicine,Investigation,Occultt</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mage can analyze then state of a metaphorical or literal fire. For each level of potency,the mage gets to ask one question,such as &quot;how long has that fire been burning?&quot;, &quot;has it hurt or inspired anyone?&quot;, &quot;what was its purpose?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hot to Handle (Fire\u25cf\u25cf)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice: Ruling</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Potency</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills:Subterfuge, Expression, Crafts</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mages emanates an aura </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That he's more trouble than he is worth. For the duration of the spell,each level of potency gives rolls to intimidate or attack you a -1 penalty</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Heat Master (Fire\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice : Weaving</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Potency </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Craft,Expression,Occult</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mage can shape heat into a physical shape. The objects can be used to melt away things or burn the target of the spell </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fire Blast (Fire\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice : Patterning </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Potency </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Craft,Expression,Firearms</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A damage spell,where each level of potency deals on level of Lethal damage</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Create Ephemera of Fire (Fire \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Practice:Making </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primary Factor: Duration</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Suggested Rote Skills: Craft,Expression,Occult </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Mage creates an ephemeral entity,Ghost goetia or spirit,which is related to the purviews of the fire arcanum. The entities is rank 1,if it's a Ghost,it stays on Twilight. The Mage cam command it without any additional spells</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aeon Of Fire:<br /> <br /> Pele is he Aeon representing Fire in the awakened cosmology,thr goddess representaz Awakening itself.<br /> <br /> Exarch of Fire:</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;The Burn is the exarch that punished people for stepping too far beyond what is Known, he keeps people near the circle of firelight, never to find any riches in the darkness beyond,curbing human progress&quot;</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-13-2022, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T03:24:58-07:00","id":1481056,"title":"","content":"Sounds a lot like what godly (Rank 6+) ephemeral entities were IIRC assumed to be capable of with Influences at 6+ dots, from <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> (1e supplement). Maybe you could check that out too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T07:43:50-07:00","id":1481069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481026-setting-hack-minor-arcana-and-realms?p=1481056#post1481056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds a lot like what godly (Rank 6+) ephemeral entities were IIRC assumed to be capable of with Influences at 6+ dots, from <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> (1e supplement). Maybe you could check that out too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna take a look!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:36:26-07:00","id":1481082,"title":"","content":"The Tamers of the Elements also sound like something to read up on, too, if only for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:42:23-07:00","id":1481084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1481026-setting-hack-minor-arcana-and-realms?p=1481082#post1481082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tamers of the Elements also sound like something to read up on, too, if only for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks,I'm gonna do just that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T09:51:57-07:00","id":1481086,"title":"","content":"Minor Supernal Realm: The Dawn,Supernal Realm of the Laos<br /> <br /> The Dawn is all about the rebirth,the thunderbolt surrounded by darkness on all sides, the sun rising In the west banishing that same darkness. Their is path is Laos,&quot;the people&quot; in latin.<br /> It's arcana are Fire and Darkness <br /> The inferior arcana is Cold<br /> <br /> Mage Sight of the Dawn.<br /> <br /> It's always a new day,the first day of your life,the last second of an old universe being consigned to darkness so a new one can be born. The Dawn is a cosmic realm,presenting visions that would make anyone who has the tiniest bit of love for the concept of outer space to weep in joy. All Arcana, &quot;major&quot; and &quot;minor&quot; can be seen here. But Fire and Darkness are seen most of all. Fire is represented by supernovas ,Darkness are Black holes. Other arcana are as follows<br /> <br /> <br /> Death : is a rite of passage,the death of stars and galaxies are not a waste,they return to the universe, it's recycling. To manipulate Death,a Laos might simply reach for a star and dim it's light<br /> Cold: is complicated In the Dawn,it undercuts it's main philosophy,that the universe holds you in a warm embrace. A Laos needs to look to the coldest part of their personality to manipulate this minor Arcanun<br /> Fate: is a big mess of chaos,a positive mess to be sure but an extremely confusing one. To manipulate it,a Laos does something very much taking the position of a star maker,making plans for the cosmos <br /> Forces:: are nothing less than cosmic In the Dawn,planets are born,planets die. And are assaulted by natural elements. Usually the Laos breath in the sheer universal forces and breath them out.<br /> Life: All corners of the Dawn have life,it might be organic life, but it often inst. Sometimes that life doesn't seem to make sense,but it can be understood by deep thoughtful analysis<br /> <br /> Matter: Matter here is dark matter,it's malleable and huge and can be used to build damn near anything. You reach to have to reach up to the place between stars and planets<br /> Mind: show you how to navigate the Dawn, the cosmic plans of infinite alien gods are in the Mind,sometimes all it takes is a conversation<br /> Prime: Is the Dawn itself,the new beginning and the why of new beginnings. You ponder that justification to be able to reach the Truth<br /> Space: No matter how huge the Dawn is,there's always Space, the connections In here are about how the Wings of a butterfly in a tiny planet can cause blessings Light years away. Just nudge the butterfly and the infinite connections will bring on the blessings<br /> Spirit: Everything moves In the Dawn,even the seemingly static objects move. It's like a dance,the spirits dance with the cosmos,you have to join the dance and feel the spirit of yourself move with the others.<br /> Time: is a good way to measure the new beginnings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-14-2022, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T10:30:36-07:00","id":1481092,"title":"","content":"Minor Arcanum: Cycles<br /> Purview: Rebirth,circles, Ephemeral Entities with Influence(Rebirth)<br /> <br /> It takes a lot of esoteric thought to truly understand the Arcanum of cyclesit overlaps with at least four others while still being it's own power. Cycles are about the beginning, middle an end. of things. an endless repeating circle. In mythology,gods associated with cycles include the spirits of Slavic folk religion,and the titan Kronos.<br /> <br /> Sample spell for the cycles Arcanum<br /> <br /> Movement(Cycles \u2022)<br /> Practice: Compelling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Expression,Socialize Occult.<br /> The mage can help himself or others who are stuck in a rut,for each level of Potency,the subject of the spell can +2 bonus on any rolls to find a new way to get out of a difficult situation.<br /> <br /> Ward Against The Wheel (Cycles \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Shielding<br /> Primary factor: potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills:Athletics,Occult,Subterfuge<br /> The Mage can now protect himself against harmful cycles ,effects that would age the Mage,or force to be moved in a different way, gain a -2 penalty for each dot of potency of the spell.<br /> <br /> Transform the Cycle (Cycles \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Weaving<br /> Primary factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft, Expression, Occult<br /> <br /> The mage can turn a cycle, something bthst could be classified as something that has a beginning,middle and end that renews itself into something else for the duration of the spell. Examples include,shifting the way a minor election is decided,or influencing the way crops grow. This last during the duration of the spell<br /> <br /> Break the Wheel(Cycles \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Practice: Unraveling<br /> Primary Spell factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft,Subterfuge,Larceny<br /> Cycles can't be broken really easily,it takes precision. A mage using this spell can simply stop cycles of any kind for the bapells duration. Examples including, stopping the wheels of a vehicle,or even disrupting a building energy distribution<br /> <br /> Create Circle (Cycles \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Making<br /> Primary Effect: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Craft Expression Socialize<br /> <br /> Where there was nothing,suddenly there was something. A entire new cycle can be created ex nihilo. Example include, making new ideas surge after a brand fart moment,or fixing irreparable machines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}